 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? You can pick them up at the store and keep them in the fridge until you get home, or order in if you have a reliable delivery option. If you keep them a closed container in the fridge, they'll stay fresh for several days. Keep them in a box with a window so the air can get at them without the wind blowing on the bag. Or use a windproof bag if you' camping. You could have always said steak. It's a great way to spice up an evening. Then at least ask at the shop if you can see the steaks in person. Many shops do show room tours now and then.",
